{
 "title": "Enums und match",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Ein **`enum`** listet die Möglichkeiten (**Varianten**) auf, die ein Wert annehmen kann. Um einen Enum-Wert anzuschauen, verwendest du **`match`**. Das Wichtigste daran: Der Compiler prüft, dass **alle Fälle** behandelt werden. Vergisst du eine Variante, kompiliert der Code nicht."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn action(light: TrafficLight):",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            print(\"Stop!\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Yellow:",
    "            print(\"Get ready...\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Green:",
    "            print(\"Go!\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Red)",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Green)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Stop!",
    "Go!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Wenn du nicht alle einzeln hinschreiben willst, fängt `_:` alles Übrige."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn is_stop(light: TrafficLight) -> bool:",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            return true",
    "        _:",
    "            return false",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(is_stop(TrafficLight.Red), is_stop(TrafficLight.Yellow))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "true false"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c06-l01-x1",
   "prompt": "Schreibe für das Enum `Direction` (`North`, `South`, `East`, `West`) `name(d)`: Es gibt den eigenen Namen aus (`north`, `south`...). Rufe es für `West` auf.",
   "starter": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        _:",
    "            print(\"?\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        Direction.South:",
    "            print(\"south\")",
    "        Direction.East:",
    "            print(\"east\")",
    "        Direction.West:",
    "            print(\"west\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "hint": "Schreibe für jede Variante einen Zweig; lass das `_` weg.",
   "expected": [
    "west"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c06-l01-q1",
   "q": "Was passiert, wenn du in `match` eine Variante vergisst?",
   "options": [
    "Es stürzt zur Laufzeit ab",
    "Der Code kompiliert nicht",
    "Sie wird stillschweigend übersprungen"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`match` ist erschöpfend: Ein fehlender Fall ist ein Kompilierfehler."
  }
 ]
}
